{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Clarification research applied to the plan. Current mutmut/PyPI is 3.7.0; it adds per-function and caller cache invalidation plus config/dependency tracking. Important hazard: mutmut excludes Python files from its default non-source dependency scan, so a restored cache can miss modified tests unless mapped tests are explicit cache-invalidation inputs or selected mutants are forcibly rerun. The revised design does both, never skips evaluation on an exact cache hit, and uses a diagnostic-only rerun that cannot turn a failure green. The seven shard budgets now come directly from the checked-in June/July measurements. Weekly broad execution is retained as the low-cost backstop for mapping/tool drift; Gerrit remains the blocking changed-shard path."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786419648294819001,"uuid":"88551061-5c87-4164-8c1d-eaad5632593e"}